# Workspace Venv Fallback

RULE: If a repo's local venv (e.g. `.venv`) isn't working — missing deps, wrong Python, import errors — using the workspace venv is fine.

WHY: Repo venvs can be out of sync or missing transitive deps (e.g. google-cloud-pubsub, unified-feature-calculator). The workspace venv (`.venv-workspace`) is shared and typically has all deps installed.

## Workspace venv name

The workspace venv is always named `.venv-workspace` across workspaces. Use:

```bash
source .venv-workspace/bin/activate
```

or from workspace root:

```bash
cd $WORKSPACE_ROOT && source .venv-workspace/bin/activate
```

Use workspace venv when: repo venv has missing deps, wrong Python, or cross-repo commands needed.

DO: Use for pytest, quality gates when repo venv fails.
NEVER: Assume repo venv is always correct; never block on repo venv issues when workspace venv works.
